  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent bullish bias in reality vs model: forecasts are systematically too low during strong uptrends (late Dec–early Jan). Apply an upward level shift when recent realized prices are accelerating (e.g., last 5–10 days slope > 0).",
    "Trend-lag error: model underestimates both the magnitude and persistence of rallies; true path keeps grinding higher while forecast flattens/mean-reverts. Reduce mean-reversion strength and increase trend-following weight when price breaks above the 20–30d range.",
    "Horizon-dependent underpricing: the under-forecast grows with horizon (errors widen notably after ~day 7–10). Use a horizon ramp correction (small uplift near-term, larger uplift mid/long-term) in trending regimes.",
    "Post-spike behavior mis-specified: after upside jumps, the model often predicts pullbacks/sideways, but realized continues higher. Replace 'fade the spike' with 'partial continuation' unless there is clear reversal evidence (e.g., multiple down closes).",
    "Volatility compression: forecast path is too smooth vs realized (misses higher highs). Inflate forecast volatility/upper tail during momentum regimes (e.g., widen bands or add convex uplift proportional to recent realized volatility).",
    "Regime switch heuristic: if last price is above its 30d moving average and the MA is rising, apply momentum regime corrections (uplift + reduced reversion); otherwise keep baseline/mean-reverting behavior."
  ]
}
